{"parentUuid":"8ef8a2e7-0737-4612-8479-669fbc67b857","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffiZDCQLDFX7vDWaEwqA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QRUSzkaGo84XUbMUD76NHg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status | head -3 && ls && ls spec/capabilities | grep -E \"foreground-subagent|background-agent|background-bash\" && ls claude-mock claude-mock/e2e | head -80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_read_input_tokens":45252,"output_tokens":308,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":45252,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QRUSzkaGo84XUbMUD76NHg":{"command":"cd /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc && git status | head -3 && ls && ls spec/capabilities | grep -E \"foreground-subagent|background-agent|background-bash\" && ls claude-mock claude-mock/e2e | head -80"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01QRUSzkaGo84XUbMUD76NHg":{"cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffiZCvXmjjv8r42koCwa","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7268883e-04e8-4f50-86c6-2113573950f0","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:42:58.938Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59"}
{"parentUuid":"8ef8a2e7-0737-4612-8479-669fbc67b857","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AJeZL6AxZ4bznnkp7uRXsx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYou are one of 31 parallel agents; each takes ONE capability in the repo you are in (a git worktree of sloprail/harness-mocks). Goal: every `pending` cell of your capability's spec file (spec/capabilities/<id>.yaml) becomes real: **supported** (docs + recorded runs of the REAL harness, an adapter in the mock, tests) or **unsupported with evidence**. Recorded runs outrank docs: a run showing the behaviour (even partly) => supported, the gaps listed as `deviations`; a run showing the behaviour absent (whose scenario really attempts it) => `{supported: false, reason: <one line>, runs: [...] and/or docs: [...]}`. Never leave `pending`, never a bare `false`. Do NOT change the capability's `statement` (that needs the user's words) nor other capabilities' cells.\n2\t\n3\tA finished example, already on main: `git show f860ff3` (codex x bash-tool-result): scenario under codex-mock/snapshots/runs/<name>/setup/, captured with the harness's snapshots/capture.sh, cell in the spec file, `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>` adapter marker, `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>` test. Read it first, plus adr/capability-grounding, adr/capability-once, adr/modeled-surface, .sloprail/schemas/capability.cue, and the existing cells and tests of the same harness.\n4\t\n5\tHow things work\n6\t- Real harnesses are installed and logged in: `codex` and `cursor-agent`. Record with `<harness>-mock/snapshots/capture.sh run <name>` (the ONLY writer of snapshots/; hand-authored `setup/` = prompt.txt, hooks.json, hook scripts, optional args/env; read the script's header and the existing runs). It makes real model calls: keep prompts short, and capture only what you need (a few runs). Captures are serialised by a lock per harness; wait for it. `capture.sh doc <url>` freezes a doc page into the MANIFEST (cells cite `https://...#anchor` of a frozen page). Reuse existing runs when they already show the behaviour (cite them), else add new ones; run names are kebab-case; a new run name you create must be unique to your capability (prefix it with the capability id or a clear name) so parallel agents don't collide.\n7\t- Look at what the real harness did (events.jsonl, stream.jsonl, payloads.jsonl, transcript/) before deciding. Your own scenario must really attempt the behaviour; if the harness cannot do it (no such tool/hook/flag), record the attempt and mark the cell unsupported citing that run (and docs if they show it).\n8\t- Supported cell: the mock's adapter (<harness>-mock/) provides it, core behaviour lives once in internal/ (`// sr:capability <id>` already exists there; behaviour that differs per harness is a PARAMETER of core, never a copy). An adapter translates and decides nothing. Mark adapter code `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>`, and add e2e/unit tests marked `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>` (on tests only, in *_test.go) that replay/drive the mock into the recorded situation and assert what the recording shows (or the declared deviation). Unsupported cells have NO markers. `deviations` are `{adr, statement}`: use `adr: modeled-surface` where the mock models less than the harness does (interactive-only things, unimplemented tools/events), and `adr: capability-grounding` where the real harness itself doesn't do a part of the statement.\n9\t- Scope: if modelling the behaviour in the mock is large, model what the recordings show of it and declare the rest as modeled-surface deviations; do not fake behaviour the recordings don't show.\n10\t- CRITICAL for judges: the rules judge every capability that has a marker in any file you touch (whole file). So do NOT edit existing files that carry other capabilities' markers unless unavoidable; prefer NEW files for your adapter code and tests (new Go files must lie in a module home: see the module.yaml files / adr/modules-cover-code; internal/ and *-mock/ code each belongs to exactly one module). If you must touch a file with other markers, expect the judges to also re-judge those pairs and be ready to satisfy them. Keep `file-size` and `layering` ADR limits. Other agents work in parallel on other capabilities; touch only what yours needs; shared core edits should be small, additive, parameterised.\n11\t- Verify: `go build ./... && go vet ./...`, tests of what you touched (`go test -count=1 ./<harness>-mock/... ./internal/... ./tools/...`; e2e suites build the mock themselves), gofmt. Then commit (signed commits are on; message body ends with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`), `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` (conflicts, e.g. MANIFEST.yaml, are plain merges: keep both sides; if a rebase changes snapshot files, never hand-edit sealed samples), then run the repo's checks: `sr-checks run --base origin/main --head HEAD` (runs judges with a model, ~1-3 min; it caches by content; repeat until it prints no refusals). Read each refusal and fix the cause (a test that doesn't assert what the recording shows, a deviation that is false, a cell not shown by its citations...). A refusal about something clearly pre-existing and unrelated to your change: report it rather than rewriting other capabilities.\n12\t- Merge: `git push -u origin HEAD`, `gh pr create --base main` (title \"<harness>: <id> ...\"; body ends with \"🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\"), wait for CI (`gh pr checks <n> --watch`), and when ALL checks pass: `gh pr merge <n> --squash --admin` (the user authorised admin-merge when CI passes). If main moved meanwhile and CI/verify fails on a stale base, rebase, re-run sr-checks, push --force-with-lease, and retry. Never merge with a failing check.\n13\t- Do not touch other worktrees, never use bare `git stash`, never `cd` out of your worktree.\n14\t\n15\tFinal report (short): per cell: supported/unsupported, runs captured, what you implemented, PR number and merge status, anything left red and why.\n16\t\n17\tCapture gotcha (cursor): the installed `cursor-agent` may be newer (2026.10.01) than snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml's version (2026.09.28), and capture.sh refuses. Do NOT run `capture.sh all`. Instead put the 2026.09.28 build on PATH for the capture: look in `~/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/` for the directory of that version and prepend it to PATH (`PATH=<dir>:$PATH cursor-mock/snapshots/capture.sh run <name>`; check `cursor-agent --version` prints 2026.09.28 first).\n18\t"}]},"uuid":"890bd96f-0d4c-44ae-b92d-ed4308e88b1b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:42:59.139Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8ef8a2e7-0737-4612-8479-669fbc67b857","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59"}
{"parentUuid":"7268883e-04e8-4f50-86c6-2113573950f0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRUSzkaGo84XUbMUD76NHg","type":"tool_result","content":"On branch worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\nCLA.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nadr\nclaude-mock\ncodex-mock\ncursor-mock\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\nproposals\nspec\ntools\nbackground-agent.yaml\nbackground-bash-reaped-at-exit.yaml\nbackground-bash.yaml\nforeground-subagent-bash-ends-with-response.yaml\nforeground-subagent-result.yaml\nprint-waits-for-background-agents.yaml\nclaude-mock:\nMakefile\ne2e\ne2etest\ninternal\nmain.go\nrun.go\nrun_flags.go\nsnapshots\n\nclaude-mock/e2e:\n001_passthrough\n002_hooks\n002_worktree\n003_session\n003_toolexec\n004_subagent\n005_pretooluse\n006_posttooluse\n007_toolexec\n008_session_file\n009_agent_tool\n010_subagent_block_loop\n011_plugin_hooks\n012_schedule_wakeup\n013_compaction\n014_sragent_flags\n015_resume_prompt\n016_transcript_chain\n017_session_lifecycle","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cffdd0ac-8786-48b6-a109-ea61264040c3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:42:59.479Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7268883e-04e8-4f50-86c6-2113573950f0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59"}
