{"parentUuid":"ab790001-b11c-462a-bc02-6f4c12e8532e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TVrWUCdGCGo8PcKtRkRfCs","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A foreground sub-agent blocks its parent until it finishes, then hands its\n  final report back as the tool's result with a trailer naming the sub-agent\n  and its usage.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#run-subagents-in-foreground-or-background\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference#agent-tool-behavior\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/meta\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookmix\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\nstatement: >-\n  A sub-agent can be dispatched in the background: the agent gets a receipt at\n  once, and the sub-agent runs concurrently with the turn that launched it.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#run-subagents-in-foreground-or-background\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\nstatement: >-\n  A shell command can be started in the background: the agent gets a receipt\n  at once naming the task and the file its output goes to, and the command\n  keeps running while the agent works.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference#background-commands\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgbash\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/midturn\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock does not model a background command's time limit: the docs\n          give 30 minutes by default, or the timeout passed with\n          run_in_background up to 2 hours (raised by BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS and\n          BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS), and a stop notice reading 'Background command\n          \"<description>\" was stopped after reaching its background time\n          limit'. A mock's background command runs until it ends or the session\n          reaps it.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock does not model a foreground command moving to the\n          background: the docs say one that reaches its timeout is moved to the\n          background ('Command did not complete within its 120s timeout and was\n          moved to the background', with the task id and output file), and that\n          a foreground sub-agent's moved command still stops when that\n          sub-agent's run ends. A mock's foreground command is never moved.\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*_test.go","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"23ea130a-8e62-4aa1-83ed-f88ed277f8cf","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:43:01.835Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ab790001-b11c-462a-bc02-6f4c12e8532e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59"}
