{"parentUuid":"660d2b3b-3095-4fdc-8dcc-ad04fdd767c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012cCPEqDkrdW3U9pRNsTbHf","type":"tool_result","content":"sloprail: judging \"adr-conformance\" changeset with \"../../_lib/adr-conforms.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-grounded\" background-agent with \"./docs-support-statement.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-grounded\" foreground-subagent-result with \"./docs-support-statement.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" background-agent with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" background-bash with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" background-bash-reaped-at-exit with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judged \"capability-grounded\" background-agent in 30s\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" foreground-subagent-result with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judged \"capability-grounded\" foreground-subagent-result in 38s\nsloprail: judged \"capability-rigor\" background-bash in 38s\nsloprail: judged \"adr-conformance\" changeset in 39s\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" noninteractive-run with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"concern-undeclared\" changeset with \"./classify.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" print-waits-for-background-agents with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judged \"capability-rigor\" background-bash-reaped-at-exit in 46s\nsloprail: judging \"invariant-rigor\" turn-loop with \"./tests-prove-statement.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judged \"capability-rigor\" background-agent in 56s\nsloprail: judging \"module-leaks\" internal/tools with \"./leak-or-use.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judged \"capability-rigor\" print-waits-for-background-agents in 24s\nsloprail: judged \"invariant-rigor\" turn-loop in 18s\nsloprail: judged \"module-leaks\" internal/tools in 14s\nsloprail: judged \"capability-rigor\" noninteractive-run in 41s\nsloprail: judged \"concern-undeclared\" changeset in 55s\nsloprail: judged \"capability-rigor\" foreground-subagent-result in 1m15s\nthe following rules refused this work:\n  - capability-once: claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go agentRunsInBackground re-implements the background decision (the `if cfg.BackgroundTasksDisabled { return false }` gate plus the definition's `background: true` override) in the adapter, replacing the core tasks.RunsInBackground call in stream_turn.go, and agent_limit.go/stream_hook.go put the maxTurns stop decision (turnLimit.Step, ending the run, suppressing SubagentStop) in claude-mock; this breaks 'An adapter translates and decides nothing: when a hook fires, ... and in what order things happen are the capability's' and 'A capability's behaviour lives once, in internal/'. Move the turn-limit, background-override and tool-stats logic into internal/ (tasks/subagents) marked sr:capability, pass the frontmatter values as parameters, and keep tasks.RunsInBackground as the gate. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - Capabilities not implemented, adapted or proven (adr/capability-once):\n- capability 'foreground-subagent-result' needs exactly one // sr:capability foreground-subagent-result, in internal/ (found 2)\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/recorded_helpers_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_limit.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_prepare.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_result.go (and 89 more) (file-guard \"capability-covered\")\n  - The listed tests leave two doc behaviours uncovered. (1) Sub-agents doc, 'Let subagents spawn their own subagents': in non-interactive -p mode a launching sub-agent does not wait for its nested background sub-agent, and a nested one that finishes after its launcher ended reports to the main conversation. Only test_017_02f_nested_background_test.go checks this, and it is not marked `sr:proves background-agent/claude` or listed for this subject. (2) The 'Concurrent subagent limit' section says that with 20 sub-agents running, a spawn fails with `Concurrent subagent limit reached`, and CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS changes the limit. No test or mock code mentions it and no <deviation> declares it. The recorded bgagent and bgagent-definition runs, the receipt, hook order, Stop background_tasks, notification, `background: true` definition and DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS cases are otherwise well covered. Fix: add `sr:proves background-agent/claude` to the nested-background test and add a test (or a deviation) for the concurrent-limit refusal.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_limit.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_prepare.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_result.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_run.go (and 86 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - test_017_61 'with_description' asserts PreToolUse/PostToolUse tool_input carries description (\"quick echo\"), and its comment claims bgbash recorded the input with a description, but the bgbash sample's PreToolUse/PostToolUse tool_input is {\"command\":\"sleep 8; echo BGDONE\",\"run_in_background\":true} with no description (even though Stop's background_tasks shows description \"long sleep\"), so the test pins a value the recording contradicts.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_limit.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_prepare.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_result.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_run.go (and 86 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The sub-agents doc (Subagent output scanning, line 943) names two imitation variants that get a backslash, a line starting with `Human:` and one starting with `Assistant:`. The mock implements both (`role-line` in internal/runner/agent_scan.go), but TestT017_70_AgentReportIsScannedBeforeTheParentReadsIt only drives `Human:` (fgsub-report-scan-role), so no test covers `Assistant:`. Add a test, and a recorded run, for a report with an `Assistant:` line. Separately, the foreground task_notification frame's summary for a scanned report (the notice plus report, recorded in fgsub-report-scan) is not asserted by any test. TestT017_25 only checks it for a clear report.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_se