{"parentUuid":"5cf780b6-8210-4c5f-9d37-fb940bfa1607","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01492KrN4b6QRPdaTLs66oWx","type":"tool_result","content":"889:* **Background subagents** run concurrently while you continue working. When a background subagent reaches a tool call that needs permission, Claude Code surfaces the prompt in your main session and names the subagent that is asking. Approve to let the subagent continue, or press Esc to deny that one tool call without stopping the subagent.\n1038:### Concurrent subagent limit\n1042:By default, when 20 subagents are running in a session, spawning another with the Agent tool fails with `Concurrent subagent limit reached`, and the error tells Claude not to retry. Spawning succeeds again when the running count drops below the limit. To change the limit, set [`CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS`](/docs/en/env-vars) to any positive whole number. Sessions with [ultracode](/docs/en/model-config#adjust-effort-level) active are exempt: the limit isn't enforced there. Requires Claude Code v2.1.217 or later.\n306:| `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS` | How many [subagents](/docs/en/sub-agents#concurrent-subagent-limit) can be running in one session before the Agent tool refuses to spawn another (default: 20). Accepts a positive whole number in plain digits; anything else is ignored, so the variable can adjust the cap but can't disable it. Requires Claude Code v2.1.217 or later |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"82f06de6-c1dd-41eb-a8d5-09280b123562","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:11:35.215Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5cf780b6-8210-4c5f-9d37-fb940bfa1607","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a54d