{"parentUuid":"2266218d-1948-4d83-ad23-61d7b6ebb18d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SvGP7B5TbEaJRjw1wKZXfc","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - mock-config: claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go:26 calls os.Getenv(\"CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS\") outside the entrypoint (and the file is not in the ADR's exceptions), breaking 'No other code calls os.Getenv...' and 'reads every flag and environment variable once, in its entrypoint package'; read the variable at the entrypoint into Config (like BackgroundTasksDisabled) and pass the value to subagents.ConcurrentLimit. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - Doc-stated concurrent-limit behaviours have no e2e test marked sr:proves background-agent/claude and no declared deviation: the default limit of 20 when CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS is unset is covered only by an internal unit test (internal/subagents/limits_test.go), the e2e tests only set it to 1 and only refuse a background second launch (a foreground Agent call at the limit is never tested), and the doc rule that resuming a finished sub-agent via SendMessage takes a slot without checking the limit is neither tested nor declared a deviation; the doc line that background sub-agents get a smaller built-in tool set is also unchecked.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_02f_nested_background_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 116 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The recorded fgsub-maxturns run (events 10-19) and the tools-reference line 'Claude can resume the subagent to continue' show a maxTurns-limited agent being resumed through SendMessage: a PostToolUse for SendMessage with resumedAgentId, a second SubagentStart, the remaining Bash calls THREE and FOUR, and a task-notification whose summary says it 'stopped at its 2-turn limit (partial result; SendMessage to task-id to continue)'. TestT017_76 only compares hooks up to the first Agent PostToolUse (upTo) and asserts no THREE in the hand-back. No test covers the resume. The mock has no SendMessage resume at all (no 'Resuming agent' or resumedAgentId in claude-mock outside snapshots), and no deviation declares that gap. The rest of the checklist is covered: blocking (T017_66), the hand-back frame and trailer, toolStats, scan notices, the kept worktree, nested and isolated runs, the SubagentStop block loop, and the maxTurns note.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_02f_nested_background_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 116 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The doc (sub-agents#let-subagents-spawn-their-own-subagents, line 1011) says a fork at the depth limit keeps the Agent tool but its dispatch returns an error instead of spawning. No test covers this: test_009_20 only checks the non-fork case, where Agent is withheld and the result is 'No such tool available: Agent'. The mock does not model sub-agent forks, and the capability YAML declares no deviation for it. The other items are covered: spawnDepth and parentAgentId in the meta sidecars (T017_30), one subagents/ directory (T017_13), the default depth of 3 and the env override (T009_20 and T009_21), and the launcher not waiting in -p mode (T017_02f).\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_02f_nested_background_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 116 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - file-guard/config-at-entry (a mock reads its configuration once, at its entrypoint):\n- claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go reads or writes the process environment: read it once at the entrypoint into the configuration\n- the code outside the allowed place now holds 13 sites, up from 12: legacy sites may only be removed (file-guard \"config-at-entry\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"74730faf-4b44-41b3-bd31-56284032d76a","timestamp":"2026-