{"parentUuid":"ac5452f5-e233-4e22-be52-b2e030c88bd7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V5B6tEU5BP14Y9U1Tbug2f","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A sub-agent can be dispatched in the background: the agent gets a receipt at\n  once, and the sub-agent runs concurrently with the turn that launched it.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#run-subagents-in-foreground-or-background\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent-definition\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock does not model an in-process agent team's teammates: the docs say\n          a sub-agent a teammate spawns runs in the foreground, that spawning one\n          whose definition sets `background: true` is refused with an error, and\n          that a teammate's `run_in_background` is refused where fork mode is off.\n          Agent teams are an interactive-session feature, and so is fork mode, which\n          makes every sub-agent run in the background: a mock session is `-p`, with\n          fork mode off.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Codex's spawn_agent has no foreground or background choice: it\n          always answers at once with a receipt (the sub-agent's id and a\nhint: To abort and get back to the state before \"git rebase\", run \"git rebase --abort\".\nCould not apply ae0fcd27... claude: move the sub-agent limits, tally and scan into the core; model the concurrent sub-agent limit; cover the judges' findings","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"db48c86c-74cb-47d2-8109-453cba3fd1dc","timestam