9e3-426b-971e-874b85a887cf","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:27:35.814Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
{"parentUuid":"dbc65d61-89e3-426b-971e-874b85a887cf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J9uRk5sDWbqjxpREqdvzo9","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A sub-agent can be dispatched in the background: the agent gets a receipt at\n  once, and the sub-agent runs concurrently with the turn that launched it.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#run-subagents-in-foreground-or-background\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#concurrent-subagent-limit\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent-definition\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent-concurrent-limit\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock's executor does not implement the SendMessage tool, so it does not\n          model a finished sub-agent resumed in the background by a message, nor\n          that a resume takes a slot without the concurrent limit refusing it.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock does not take tools away from a background sub-agent: the docs\n          give it a smaller built-in tool set than a foreground one (Read, Grep,\n          Glob, LSP, Bash, Edit, Write, WebFetch, Monitor, SendMessage and a few\n          more), but every tool the docs remove from it is one the mock's\n          executor does not implement for any sub-agent.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock does not model an in-process agent team's teammates: the docs say\n          a sub-agent a teammate spawns runs in the foreground, that spawning one\n          whose definition sets `background: true` is refused with an error, and\n          that a teammate's `run_in_background` is refused where fork mode is off.\n          Agent teams are an interactive-session feature, and so is fork mode, which\n          makes every sub-agent run in the background: a mock session is `-p`, with\n          fork mode off.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock does not model the sessions the docs exempt from the concurrent\n          sub-agent limit: those with ultracode active, which is turned on through\n          the effort level in an interactive session.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Codex's spawn_agent has no foreground or background choice: it\n          always answers at once with a receipt (the sub-agent's id and a\n          nickname) and the sub-agent runs concurrently with the turn, its\ndiff --git a/spec/capabilities/foreground-subagent-result.yaml b/spec/capabilities/foreground-subagent-result.yaml\nindex e70b2728..06135fc7 100644\n--- a/spec/capabilities/foreground-subagent-result.yaml\n+++ b/spec/capabilities/foreground-subagent-result.yaml\n@@ -11,5 +11,26 @@ providers:\n       - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/meta\n       - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n       - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookmix\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/isolated-worktree\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/fgsub-report-scan\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/fgsub-report-scan-perm\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/fgsub-report-scan-role\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/fgsub-report-scan-assistant\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/fgsub-tool-stats\n+      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/fgsub-maxturns\n+    deviations:\n+      - adr: modeled-surface\n+        statement: >-\n+          The mock's executor does not implement the SendMessage tool, so it does not\n+          model resuming a finished sub-agent (or one that stopped at its maxTurns)\n+          with a message: the docs and the fgsub-maxturns recording show Claude\n+          doing it, the resumed sub-agent carrying on in the background.\n+      - adr: modeled-surface\n+        statement: >-\n+          The mock has no model API to fail: it does not model the docs' hand-back of\n+          a sub-agent cut off by an API error (a rate limit, overload or server\n+          error), which returns the partial output with a note that it was cut off,\n+          or fails with 'Agent terminated early due to an API error', and which\n+          continues a cut-off response before ending the run.\n   codex: pending\n   cursor: pending","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"48edff11-daeb-4877-b80d-c2afe476be7a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:27:36.647Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbc65d61-89e3-426b-971e-874b85a887cf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
