{"parentUuid":"3d4b9ee6-2cc7-447f-8232-879a4ac9fd2e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vkg2SZEoqzwdfb2JzASbUv","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - Two behaviours the sub-agents doc states for this capability have no test and no declared deviation: (1) a background sub-agent may leave a background Bash/PowerShell command running past its turn and Claude Code then sends the sub-agent a notification when it ends, and (2) an in-session fork started with /subtask takes a concurrent-limit slot while it runs and is never blocked by the limit (the 'Concurrent subagent limit' section). Everything else checked against the four recordings (receipt, hook order, notification, definition background:true, concurrent-limit refusal, nested launcher) is covered; add tests plus recordings for these two, or declare them as modeled-surface deviations.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_79_nested_background_report_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 132 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The headless docs state behaviours that none of the three tests exercise. They are --output-format text (the default) and json (one object with result and session metadata), --json-schema with structured_output, and the non-zero exit and failure-as-result-on-stdout path. They also state SIGTERM exiting 143 with no result, and the system/init event (with hook_* events before it) being first in the stream. The runs show a stream that begins hook_started, hook_response, init and ends with one result, but T001_01 only passes through the script's own init line and never checks that the mock emits it. Add tests, with recordings, for these; the three tests only cover stream-json passthrough, one result after Stop re-prompts, and exit 0 after a failed tool.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_79_nested_background_report_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 132 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - Recorded fork behaviours go unchecked: no test asserts that the fork's SessionStart payload carries the new session_id (events.jsonl b2 line: source \"fork\" with session_id ...0b2; the tests only compare the `source` list). No test runs --fork-session with --resume but no --session-id, so a generated id that differs from the original is never checked (the doc says the fork gets its own ID). No test runs --fork-session without --resume, which the run's c3 step records as a plain new session with source \"startup\". No test resumes the original after a fork (the ELSEWHERE step) to show it continues without the fork's turn. The fork-then-resume path is also not covered for --continue --fork-session, which the CLI doc names.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_79_nested_background_report_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 132 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestT017_31_ResumeStartPayloadCarriesTheResumeFacts (test_017_resume_payload_test.go) pins context_tokens and estimated_cache_write_usd to 0 on resume/fork SessionStart, but the recordings show non-zero values (forkresume line 7: \"context_tokens\":23551,\"estimated_cache_write_usd\":0.0471; compact line 7: 23567/0.0471) and no <deviation> declares this, so the test asserts something the real harness did not do (it should assert positive/present values instead). Also, none of the marked tests asserts that the resumed-elsewhere SessionStart/Stop/SessionEnd carry the original session_id, which the forkresume ELSEWHERE sample shows.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent