{"parentUuid":"971acbd4-10ec-49e5-a14e-ec04d827dade","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a8a444ee54a52b4dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B1v45hW1DedmaNzzKTvGfT","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - capability-once #3 (\"A capability's behaviour lives once, in internal/, on code marked `// sr:capability <id>`\"): the new core code carrying background-agent and foreground-subagent-result behaviour (internal/subagents/concurrency.go AtConcurrentLimit, limit.go TurnLimit/Limited, scan.go Scan, tally.go Tally, internal/tasks/adopt.go Registry.Adopt) has no `// sr:capability <id>` marker, while the claude-mock adapters are marked `sr:provides`; add `// sr:capability background-agent` or `// sr:capability foreground-subagent-result` on those core functions. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - The final stream `result` frame in every recording carries `subagent_stats` (spawned, requested.background, started_in_background, max_depth, refused.concurrency_limit=1 in bgagent-concurrent-limit), and no test, mock code or deviation covers it. The docs' interactive-session variant, where a launcher subagent waits for the background subagents it launched, is also neither tested nor declared as a deviation.\nThe files this refusal is about: claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_61_background_bash_hook_payloads_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_70_agent_report_scan_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_71_foreground_agent_hooks_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_73_agent_tool_stats_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_75_agent_definition_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_77_background_bash_frames_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_78_concurrent_subagent_limit_test.go, claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_79_nested_background_report_test.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_concurrency.go, claude-mock/internal/runner/agent_definition.go (and 131 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - internal/subagents/limit.go introduces the codebase's first context-carried run state (`WithLimit`: `context.WithValue(ctx, limitKey{}, l)` / `LimitOf`, used by agent_stop.go `Run(subagents.WithLimit(ctx, s.limit), subCfg)` and read in stream_turn.go `subagents.LimitOf(ctx).Step()`), which settles how a per-run setting reaches the turn loop (via context values rather than the Config fields used everywhere else, as the recent commit moving the concurrent setting from the context into a Config field shows) — no ADR decides this; ask the user to decide it (a new ADR) or which existing ADR it falls under. (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bae9656d-ae1b-4115-85e9-8d8cfd99f496","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:53:45.675Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"971acbd4-10ec-49e5-a14e-ec04d827dade","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}
